  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array AAA of length NNN, we obtain its score as follows.\n\nPerform the following operation N−2N-2N−2 times:\n\n\nIf gcd⁡(A1,A3)≤gcd⁡(A2,A3)\\gcd(A_1, A_3) \\leq \\gcd(A_2, A_3)gcd(A1​,A3​)≤gcd(A2​,A3​), delete A1A_1A1​ from AAA. Otherwise, delete A2A_2A2​.\n\nAfter the deletion, the remaining elements are re-indexed to start from 111.\nIn the end, the array will have exactly two elements remaining.\n\nIts score is defined to be the first of these two elements.\n\nFor example, consider A=[4,3,2,1]A = [4, 3, 2, 1]A=[4,3,2,1]. The process is as follows:\n\n\nFirst, gcd⁡(A1,A3)=2\\gcd(A_1, A_3) = 2gcd(A1​,A3​)=2 and gcd⁡(A2,A3)=1\\gcd(A_2, A_3) = 1gcd(A2​,A3​)=1.\n\nSince gcd⁡(A1,A3)&gt;gcd⁡(A2,A3)\\gcd(A_1, A_3) \\gt \\gcd(A_2, A_3)gcd(A1​,A3​)&gt;gcd(A2​,A3​), we delete element A2A_2A2​ from AAA.\n\nThe array is now A=[4,2,1]A = [4, 2, 1]A=[4,2,1].\nNext, gcd⁡(A1,A3)=gcd⁡(A2,A3)=1\\gcd(A_1, A_3) = \\gcd(A_2, A_3) = 1gcd(A1​,A3​)=gcd(A2​,A3​)=1.\n\nSince gcd⁡(A1,A3)≤gcd⁡(A2,A3)\\gcd(A_1, A_3) \\leq \\gcd(A_2, A_3)gcd(A1​,A3​)≤gcd(A2​,A3​), we delete element A1A_1A1​ from AAA.\n\nThe array is now A=[2,1]A = [2, 1]A=[2,1].\nThe first remaining element is 222, so that's the score of the array.\n\nYou are given three integers N,X,N, X,N,X, and YYY. Find **any** array AAA satisfying the following three conditions:\n\n\nAAA has length NNN, and consists of **distinct** integers between 111 and NNN.\nAN=XA_N = XAN​=X\nAN−1=YA_{N-1} = YAN−1​=Y\nscore(A)≠Y\\text{score}(A) \\neq Yscore(A)=Y\nIf no such array AAA exists, output −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input, containing three space-separated integers N,X,N,X,N,X, and YYY.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case:\n\n\n\nIf no valid array AAA exists, output the single integer −1-1−1 on a new line.\nOtherwise, output NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the array you found.\n\nNote that the AiA_iAi​ should be distinct integers in [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nIf there are multiple valid arrays, any of them will be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤X,Y≤N1 \\leq X, Y \\leq N1≤X,Y≤N",
      "X≠YX \\neq YX=Y",
      "The sum of NNN across all tests won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
