      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 1 2\n6 6 5\n4 4 1",
        "output": "-1\n3 1 2 4 5 6 \n3 2 1 4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: No valid array exists.\nTest case 222: Consider A=[3,1,2,4,5,6]A = [3, 1, 2, 4, 5, 6]A=[3,1,2,4,5,6]. The process is as follows:\n\ngcd⁡(3,2)=1≤gcd⁡(1,2)=1\\gcd(3, 2) = 1 \\leq \\gcd(1, 2) = 1gcd(3,2)=1≤gcd(1,2)=1. So, 333 gets deleted.\nThe array is [1,2,4,5,6][1, 2, 4, 5, 6][1,2,4,5,6].\ngcd⁡(1,4)=1\\gcd(1, 4) = 1gcd(1,4)=1 and gcd⁡(2,4)=2\\gcd(2, 4) = 2gcd(2,4)=2. So, 111 gets deleted.\nThe array is [2,4,5,6][2, 4, 5, 6][2,4,5,6].\ngcd⁡(2,5)=1\\gcd(2, 5) = 1gcd(2,5)=1 and gcd⁡(4,5)=1\\gcd(4, 5) = 1gcd(4,5)=1. So, 222 gets deleted.\nThe array is [4,5,6][4, 5, 6][4,5,6].\ngcd⁡(4,6)=2\\gcd(4, 6) = 2gcd(4,6)=2 and gcd⁡(5,6)=1\\gcd(5, 6) = 1gcd(5,6)=1. So, 555 gets deleted.\nThe array is [4,6][4, 6][4,6].\nThe process ends. The leftmost remaining element is 444, which is not equal to Y=5Y = 5Y=5 as we wanted.\n\nThere are other valid arrays, any of them will be accepted."
      }
    ]
